p.src:
We define $\begin{aligned}
T^+ &= T+R, \\
T^- &= T-R.\end{aligned}$ These are adapted to radial null motion. An ingoing radial light ray has $T^+=\text{const}$, while an outgoing radial light ray has $T^-=\text{const}$.

